<b>Episode 6


 Lost in Amusement Park</b>

01:58.880 --> 02:01.840
<b>Episode 6


 Lost in Amusement Park</b>

03:22.680 --> 03:23.760
Himuro-kun.

03:23.760 --> 03:25.640
Ch-Chief...

03:25.640 --> 03:26.900
It's good to see you.

03:26.900 --> 03:28.220
And you.

03:28.220 --> 03:30.220
Perfect timing.

03:30.230 --> 03:32.230
<b>Nekomi Land</b>

03:30.700 --> 03:31.660
Here.

03:32.830 --> 03:36.580
Two tickets... to Nekomi Land?!

03:36.580 --> 03:39.990
What do you think, Himuro-kun?

03:39.990 --> 03:41.400
A trip together...

03:43.850 --> 03:45.830
<i>Me and the chief?!</i>

03:47.670 --> 03:52.370
I received them from a client, 
but I'm not particularly interested.

03:52.370 --> 03:55.880
Oh... I see.

03:56.240 --> 03:59.380
But you appreciate cute things, don't you?

04:00.370 --> 04:04.240
I frequently see you producing 
those snowmen. As you did now.

04:04.240 --> 04:06.450
<i>It's not like I do that on purpose...</i>

04:08.640 --> 04:10.670
Oh, Fuyutsuki-san.

04:11.210 --> 04:13.920
It's good to see you, Chief.

04:13.920 --> 04:15.640
And you.

04:15.640 --> 04:19.750
Fuyutsuki-san, are you 
interested in Nekomi Land?

04:19.750 --> 04:21.650
Nekomi?

04:21.650 --> 04:22.720
Yes.

04:22.720 --> 04:25.240
You might even go together.

04:26.930 --> 04:28.680
<i>Together?!</i>

04:29.660 --> 04:31.160
Nekomi Land...

04:31.160 --> 04:33.240
I've never been there, actually.

04:33.240 --> 04:35.430
All the more reason to go, then.

04:36.360 --> 04:38.390
If you'd be satisfied with my company...

04:38.400 --> 04:40.670
A-Absolutely...

04:40.670 --> 04:42.430
Then it's decided.

04:40.670 --> 04:42.670
<b>Nekomi Land</b>

04:42.670 --> 04:42.910
<b>Nekomi Land</b>

04:43.170 --> 04:44.570
Thank you for the tickets.

04:44.570 --> 04:45.290
Not at all.

04:44.740 --> 04:46.520
Th-Thank you for the tickets!

04:46.520 --> 04:47.160
Not at all.

04:47.160 --> 04:49.170
<i>H-Heck yeah!</i>

04:49.170 --> 04:51.440
<i>The section chief's such a wingman!</i>

04:51.440 --> 04:54.400
<i>He always seemed Buddha-like to me,</i>

04:54.400 --> 04:56.940
<i>but he's a real enlightened being!</i>

04:56.940 --> 05:00.930
<i>I'm gonna worship him from now on, for sure!</i>

04:56.940 --> 05:00.930
<i>Wow, thank you! Whoa! Thanks!</i>

05:00.930 --> 05:03.680
Well... I'm looking forward to it.

05:03.680 --> 05:06.950
Y-Yes, so am I.

05:09.590 --> 05:11.530
<i>This is so awesome!</i>

05:11.530 --> 05:13.750
<i>Nekomi Land with Fuyutsuki-san...</i>

05:14.080 --> 05:16.950
<i>She said she's never been there before.</i>

05:16.950 --> 05:21.460
<i>I gotta do my research to make
 sure she has a great time!</i>

05:27.530 --> 05:28.810
Nyamero.

05:28.810 --> 05:32.720
We'll be going to Nekomi Land this Sunday.

05:32.720 --> 05:35.350
They say it's a land of love and joy featuring

05:35.230 --> 05:40.230
<b>Nekomi Land</b>

05:35.910 --> 05:38.600
the cat characters Nickey and Ninnie.

05:51.860 --> 05:53.180
Oh, what's this?

05:53.180 --> 05:54.840
Nekomi Land?

05:54.840 --> 05:56.610
Who're you going with?

05:58.320 --> 05:59.840
Fuyutsuki-san.

06:00.240 --> 06:04.250
Like a date?! That's so great!

06:04.250 --> 06:06.860
N-No... It's not a date, exactly...

06:06.860 --> 06:08.960
What an awesome setup!

06:08.960 --> 06:12.520
I can teach you all the ins and outs!

06:12.520 --> 06:15.010
I'm an AP holder!

06:15.270 --> 06:18.120
AP? Is that an annual pass?

06:18.120 --> 06:19.260
Yeah!

06:19.260 --> 06:22.710
I can park up any time, 
even just to buy a pen!

06:22.710 --> 06:24.200
"P-Park up"?

06:24.200 --> 06:27.770
It means entering the park!

06:28.100 --> 06:29.520
<i>She's an expert!</i>

06:29.870 --> 06:32.720
By the way, who's your fave?

06:32.720 --> 06:36.080
Is it Ninnie? Or Nickey?!

06:36.080 --> 06:38.280
<i>Wh-Where was she keeping those?</i>

06:38.280 --> 06:45.790
Oh, and... Whose dance do you want to see 
when the floats stop at that point in the parade?

06:45.790 --> 06:48.550
<i>Floats? Dance?</i>

06:48.550 --> 06:51.690
I'm a total show parade squatter!

06:51.690 --> 06:54.280
And the midsummer parade 
got rained out twice,

06:54.290 --> 06:57.550
but the third time, I finally got to see it!

06:57.550 --> 06:59.430
Oh, are you gonna ride rides?

06:59.430 --> 07:01.690
Or go for the meet-and-greets?

06:59.670 --> 07:03.550
<i>I'm such a novice, the jargon 
all sounds like gibberish...</i>

07:03.550 --> 07:05.520
This might be too much for me.

07:05.520 --> 07:07.560
I'm getting discouraged.

07:09.380 --> 07:12.570
Don't be like that! Give it your best shot!

07:12.570 --> 07:17.570
Nekomi's a fun time! You should go!

07:17.850 --> 07:22.080
Komori-san, you're a fan of Nekomi Land?

07:22.080 --> 07:24.060
Would you like tickets?

07:26.100 --> 07:27.340
No, no!

07:27.340 --> 07:28.430
I'm just fine!

07:28.430 --> 07:30.580
I'm an annual passholder!

07:30.580 --> 07:32.880
<i>Stare.</i>

07:32.880 --> 07:37.100
<i>Close one! I almost got on 
Himuro-kun's bad side forever!</i>

07:37.650 --> 07:40.110
Shall we make it a threesome, then?

07:41.360 --> 07:43.100
<i>Himuro-kun, I'm sorry!</i>

07:46.270 --> 07:49.380
Y-You join us too, Saejima-kun!

07:51.480 --> 07:53.600
Three's a crowd, know what I mean?

07:55.370 --> 07:57.000
Well...

07:57.490 --> 07:59.870
I'm sorry, Himuro-san.

08:00.620 --> 08:02.250
That sounds very exciting.

08:09.740 --> 08:11.880
Yes, it does.

08:13.360 --> 08:14.890
<i>He's so easy!</i>

08:29.650 --> 08:33.240
I haven't been here in forever. 
This is pretty exciting!

08:33.240 --> 08:36.400
Just leave the whole thing to me!

08:39.910 --> 08:43.160
<b>Nekomi Land
 Guidebook</b>

08:40.340 --> 08:43.160
It's twice as big as I thought.

08:43.160 --> 08:44.920
And crowded...

08:46.190 --> 08:48.320
There are so many people.

08:52.610 --> 08:53.670
Oh?

08:53.920 --> 08:56.520
I think that child is lost.

08:56.520 --> 08:58.170
Oh, it looks that way.

09:01.390 --> 09:02.770
What's wrong?

09:06.610 --> 09:08.440
Are you looking for someone?

09:09.760 --> 09:11.940
My mom and dad.

09:12.900 --> 09:15.590
Can I take you to the lost child center?

09:15.980 --> 09:16.950
Uh-huh...

09:17.830 --> 09:21.200
<i>Fuyutsuki-san's so nice.</i>

09:21.200 --> 09:25.200
First, let's get priority tickets to the shows!

09:26.400 --> 09:27.440
Eh?

09:27.440 --> 09:30.200
Where are Himuro-kun and Fuyutsuki-san?!

09:39.780 --> 09:41.220
<i>A lost child?</i>

09:42.030 --> 09:45.200
<i>Maybe we should give them some alone time.</i>

09:46.800 --> 09:48.150
Let's go on without them.

09:49.530 --> 09:52.220
We're all adults here. We'll work it out.

09:52.620 --> 09:54.230
You sure about that?

09:57.810 --> 10:00.240
What, you don't like going
 around with just me?

10:02.240 --> 10:04.830
Oh, c'mon! Where'd that come from?!

10:04.830 --> 10:07.180
Don't sound so cool!

10:07.630 --> 10:09.760
<i>It was a serious question!</i>

10:09.750 --> 10:12.750
<b>Lost Child Center</b>

10:10.790 --> 10:12.740
Thank you so much!

10:13.180 --> 10:15.760
We'll handle things from here.

10:22.640 --> 10:26.770
I'll stay with her until her family arrives.

10:29.770 --> 10:33.030
We can meet up later, Himuro-kun.

10:33.510 --> 10:35.270
I'll stay, as well!

10:36.840 --> 10:38.600
Thank you.

10:43.940 --> 10:46.980
Hello! I'm Ninnie!

10:48.790 --> 10:52.670
<i>Fuyutsuki-san sure is nice!</i>

10:58.690 --> 11:00.790
It's a snowman!

11:00.790 --> 11:02.840
Wow, wow, wow!

11:02.840 --> 11:05.310
She seems to like it.

11:08.320 --> 11:09.800
I think so.

11:12.050 --> 11:14.750
Yeah! Yeah!

11:14.750 --> 11:16.810
Thank you!

11:20.320 --> 11:22.470
I'm so glad they found her.

11:22.470 --> 11:24.080
Yes.

11:25.000 --> 11:27.840
I wonder where the other two got off to.

11:34.340 --> 11:35.790
Himuro-san?

11:38.940 --> 11:40.840
You're not gonna answer?

11:41.370 --> 11:42.590
Again...

11:43.240 --> 11:45.360
You don't like going around with just me?

11:47.110 --> 11:48.720
Oh, you!

11:48.720 --> 11:51.100
Knock it off already!

11:51.100 --> 11:54.390
Take that, and that, and that!

11:51.610 --> 11:54.390
Hey, cut it out! That hurts!

11:57.980 --> 12:00.240
<b></b>Saejima-kun

11:57.980 --> 12:00.240
<b></b>No Response

12:00.240 --> 12:02.510
He's not answering.

12:02.510 --> 12:04.060
Neither is Komori-san.

12:06.210 --> 12:09.000
I suppose we're the lost ones this time.

12:10.740 --> 12:13.140
I'm sorry, Himuro-kun.

12:14.270 --> 12:17.500
You were clearly looking 
forward to Nekomi Land.

12:17.500 --> 12:20.680
But I made you come with me
 to the lost child center...

12:20.680 --> 12:23.510
I should have just gone on my own.

12:23.510 --> 12:24.670
Not at all.

12:24.670 --> 12:27.520
I had fun at the lost child center.

12:27.520 --> 12:32.050
And... I'm enjoying myself now, too.

12:33.630 --> 12:36.800
Just watching the people 
here acting so happy

12:38.060 --> 12:40.960
makes me happy, as well.

12:44.370 --> 12:46.180
That's a relief to hear.

12:47.700 --> 12:52.400
It's my first time at Nekomi Land, 
but it seems like a nice place.

12:52.400 --> 12:53.410
Yes.

12:54.040 --> 12:57.210
Nickey and Ninnie are cute, aren't they?

12:57.210 --> 13:00.540
Yes. As is George the Kitten.

13:01.880 --> 13:04.070
All cats are cute.

13:06.520 --> 13:08.210
Yes, they are!

13:08.210 --> 13:11.050
And that goes for Nyamero too, of course!

13:13.060 --> 13:14.120
Yes.

13:15.060 --> 13:19.060
<i>But nothing's cuter than Fuyutsuki-san!</i>

13:21.830 --> 13:22.800
Is there...

13:22.800 --> 13:24.060
Oh, nothing.

13:24.060 --> 13:27.070
Papa! This way!

13:26.050 --> 13:27.070
Watch it!

13:36.160 --> 13:38.320
Hey, you're all right.

13:38.320 --> 13:41.370
Pain, pain, go away!

13:41.370 --> 13:42.950
It doesn't hurt.

13:42.950 --> 13:44.870
I'm okay, I promise!

13:45.320 --> 13:47.210
Thanks for the help!

13:47.210 --> 13:48.620
Bye-bye!

13:48.620 --> 13:50.090
Bye-bye!

13:51.680 --> 13:53.360
Himuro-kun...

13:55.140 --> 13:57.110
You'd make a good father.

13:59.890 --> 14:03.860
The lost girl enjoyed your company, as well.

14:04.140 --> 14:07.000
The snowman did the heavy lifting there.

14:12.590 --> 14:14.960
Where shall we go now?

14:20.630 --> 14:23.000
According to my research,

14:23.000 --> 14:26.970
the best place to go is the Nyangoro Cruise.

14:26.970 --> 14:28.970
Nyangoro Cruise?

14:29.520 --> 14:36.840
A boat ride that presents lazy cats 
from all around the world.

14:36.840 --> 14:39.510
That sounds nice. Let's try it.

14:45.600 --> 14:46.720
So cute!

14:47.260 --> 14:49.040
I know that one!

15:06.720 --> 15:08.530
It's very cute, isn't it?

15:08.530 --> 15:09.600
Yes.

15:11.120 --> 15:13.560
Doesn't that one look like Nyamero?

15:14.380 --> 15:15.990
It certainly does!

15:43.340 --> 15:45.130
Papa, I got us a table right here!

15:45.130 --> 15:46.080
Come on!

15:47.320 --> 15:49.690
Look at them!

15:58.920 --> 16:02.100
<i>I'm no fan of crowds...</i>

16:03.440 --> 16:05.720
<i>But being here with Fuyutsuki-san...</i>

16:07.860 --> 16:11.360
<i>makes Nekomi so much fun!</i>

16:11.960 --> 16:14.080
Snow?!

16:29.390 --> 16:34.840
What you said earlier today... 
It really resonates with me.

16:35.970 --> 16:38.520
There are so many people here,

16:38.520 --> 16:41.950
and they all seem like they're
 having fun, like they're happy.

16:44.240 --> 16:48.390
Just watching them makes me happy, too.

16:50.750 --> 16:52.150
Yes!

16:54.190 --> 16:59.220
Nekomi Land truly is a land of love and joy.

17:05.130 --> 17:06.400
<i>Nekomi...</i>

17:06.400 --> 17:09.320
<i>It's the best place ever!</i>

17:10.160 --> 17:11.450
Snow!

17:11.450 --> 17:13.180
Whoa, pretty!

17:14.000 --> 17:15.560
Nekomi Land is so magical!

17:15.560 --> 17:17.170
They know how to put on a show!

17:18.320 --> 17:20.500
Well done, Himuro-kun.

17:20.500 --> 17:22.500
I'm sorry about that.

17:34.570 --> 17:38.100
Should we look at souvenirs 
while we're here?

17:38.100 --> 17:39.200
I suppose.

17:40.480 --> 17:42.270
What should I get?

17:45.440 --> 17:47.200
<i>What's this stick thing?</i>

17:49.880 --> 17:51.690
<i>It lights up and spins.</i>

17:52.850 --> 17:54.670
What about these?

17:56.220 --> 17:57.870
Mugs...

17:58.440 --> 18:00.630
We could get a matching set, 
to remember the trip.

18:01.310 --> 18:03.220
<i>Matching set?!</i>

18:03.220 --> 18:05.480
E-Excellent idea.

18:05.480 --> 18:07.340
We can use them at the office, too.

18:08.220 --> 18:09.910
If we use them at the office...

18:13.030 --> 18:16.480
Won't people talk?

18:17.020 --> 18:19.480
<i>Heck yeah, they will! Let 'em talk!</i>

18:21.540 --> 18:23.240
Himuro-kun?

18:26.240 --> 18:28.880
Er... Fuyutsuki-san?

18:31.650 --> 18:32.750
I...

18:42.840 --> 18:44.260
I...

18:45.560 --> 18:48.270
Lost children found!

18:48.520 --> 18:51.180
Komori-san. Saejima-kun.

18:51.180 --> 18:53.780
Where have you been?

18:54.490 --> 18:57.260
Not that we looked all that hard...

18:57.260 --> 18:59.090
You weren't even looking?

18:59.790 --> 19:03.240
The parade's starting soon, y'know!

19:03.240 --> 19:06.360
You should finish up your shopping quick!

19:06.360 --> 19:07.790
Oh. Of course.

19:21.570 --> 19:23.090
It's beautiful.

19:24.080 --> 19:27.310
Look! It's starting!

19:34.750 --> 19:36.320
Fireworks!

19:41.040 --> 19:43.830
They never stop being beautiful!

19:44.450 --> 19:47.640
We saw fireworks in Okinawa, too.

19:47.640 --> 19:48.920
Yes.

19:48.920 --> 19:52.340
I didn't expect to see them 
as a group again so soon.

19:52.340 --> 19:55.240
C'mon, everyone! Look this way!

20:04.690 --> 20:07.130
This was kind of a repeat of Okinawa, huh?

20:07.130 --> 20:08.720
Yeah, kinda!

20:23.360 --> 20:28.340
Fuyutsuki-san! We went on all the rides!

20:28.340 --> 20:32.200
Scheduled down to the 
minute... I'm exhausted.

20:32.200 --> 20:34.870
C'mon, don't be like that!

20:35.700 --> 20:38.200
You don't like going to them all?

20:53.990 --> 20:55.700
I had fun.

21:05.520 --> 21:08.420
Nyamero, I'm back.

21:09.740 --> 21:11.910
Thank you for watching the house.

21:11.910 --> 21:14.710
I bought you a souvenir from Nekomi Land.

21:17.640 --> 21:18.760
Ta-da.

21:18.760 --> 21:21.280
It's a Nickey and Ninnie cat toy.

21:21.280 --> 21:22.920
We can play with it later.

21:34.310 --> 21:36.170
The Nekomi mug.

21:38.690 --> 21:40.450
And...

21:38.690 --> 21:47.200
<b>George the Kitten</b>

21:44.010 --> 21:47.200
And... the George plate.

21:53.800 --> 21:57.180
<i>We have two matching sets.</i>

23:33.950 --> 23:34.980
A...

23:35.290 --> 23:37.130
A billion yen?!
